--- a/AUTO_RESUME_AND_DRAFTING_V7_0_69.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/AUTO_RESUME_AND_DRAFTING_V7_0_69.md	2026-10-20 11:21:38.000000000 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+# AutoVideo v7.0.69: automatic resume, channel setup and drafting models
+
+## What changed
+
+**1. Unattended automatic resume.** A production that stops on a recoverable Flow
+interruption (browser page closed while downloading, temporary network loss,
+Flow Agent at high demand) no longer waits for a manual Resume.
+
+- Recoverable browser and network failures in strict Flow frame generation go back
+  through the existing bounded recovery loop instead of ending the job as failed.
+- When that loop runs out of retries, the job is recorded in `auto_resume.json`
+  and a background supervisor in the Studio process resumes it after a growing
+  delay: 2, 5, 10, 20, 30, then 60 minutes between attempts, up to 8 automatic
+  resumes. The count restarts when saved media advances.
+- Never retried automatically: sign-in or quota problems, approval or changed-media
+  stops, a Flow request that was submitted but whose result is unknown (it may
+  already have used credits), and any run where you turned automatic recovery off
+  or chose to pause.
+- The job monitor shows the minutes until the next attempt and the attempt number.
+
+Limits: the supervisor runs only while Studio is open and the computer is awake.
+If the laptop sleeps or the dashboard closes, nothing runs until it is back. Keep
+the computer plugged in and set it not to sleep, and start the dashboard when you
+leave the house.
+
+**2. Channel name and logo in Create.**
+
+- The channel name and logo prompts at the end of Create follow the language
+  profiles chosen in Language editions and channel profiles (step 3).
+- When every selected edition has a profile, those prompts are hidden. The form
+  says the name and logo come from the profiles.
+- For any edition without a profile, Create asks for its channel name and logo in
+  that language, with an optional logo upload. Each entry is saved as that
+  edition's channel profile when you create the production. A blank name means
+  that edition has no channel mark.
+- With a single language and no profile, the original channel name and logo fields
+  are shown.
+
+**3. Script drafting with more models.** The "Draft script + suggest saved cast"
+button has a Drafting model selector:
+
+- Gemini Web (signed-in browser session, unchanged, default)
+- ChatGPT / OpenAI API (`OPENAI_API_KEY`)
+- Gemini API (`GEMINI_API_KEY`)
+- Groq (`GROQ_API_KEY`)
+- xAI Grok (`XAI_API_KEY`)
+- Ollama on this computer (`OLLAMA_BASE_URL`)
+
+A provider without its key is shown as not configured and is disabled. Each
+draft records the model that wrote it (`drafted_by`). The model name for each
+provider comes from its existing environment setting (for example
+`OPENAI_SCRIPT_MODEL`). ChatGPT in a signed-in browser session, like Gemini Web,
+is not part of this release.
+
+## Install
+
+Apply to an installed 7.0.68 folder:
+
+    python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.69/tools/update_v768_to_v769.py .            # dry run
+    python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.69/tools/update_v768_to_v769.py . --apply
+
+An install still on 7.0.67 must first run the 7.0.68 updater.
+Stop the dashboard before applying, then restart it.
+Outputs, jobs, browser profiles, music, characters and channel profiles are not touched.
+
+## Verification
+
+- 24 new tests (`tests/test_v769_*`): recovery classification and backoff, budget
+  reset on progress, supervisor scheduling, job-thread state, Create channel
+  branding on the real page, and drafting providers.
+- Full suite: 1242 passed, 24 failed. The same 24 fail on the untouched 7.0.68 tree
+  (environment-dependent card typography, upload picker and dashboard tests).
+- Not tested live: Flow browser behaviour, the ChatGPT/OpenAI API call itself
+  (needs your key), and a real overnight unattended run.
